According to the verified campus documents, the fees and refund policy is as follows:

1. The school charges reasonable fees as approved by CHED and allows payment on an installment plan.
2. A student who withdraws or cancels enrollment after paying one or more installments is responsible for settling the unpaid balance of fees for the whole semester.
3. A student who withdraws or cancels enrollment may be given a refund of:
   - 100% of tuition fees and other school fees except for the registration fee if he/she cancels enrollment before the scheduled start of classes;
   - 75% of tuition fees if he/she drops during the first week of classes;
   - 50% of tuition if he/she drops during the second week of classes;
   - No refund will be given to a student who withdraws any time after the second week of classes.

(Source: Chapter 4 Fees and Scholarship Policy Statement)

